    "Server busy/idle cycle (agents)": {
      "info": {
        "description": "A single Server agent alternating Idle (waiting EXPO(1/lambda) for the next customer) and Busy (serving for EXPO(1/mu)) -- the busy/idle process of an M/M/1 queue's server, without tracking the waiting line itself. Memorylessness makes each state's mean sojourn exactly 1/rate: with lambda=0.8, mu=1.0, Idle averages 1.25 and Busy averages 1.0 -- the same identity Little's law rests on. The arrival and service rates are this instance's own; add a queue-length agent type (states 0..K, arrival/departure transitions) for the waiting line itself.",
